## ★ PLAN SOUNDNESS REVIEW (standard + architecture tiers) ★

After the PLAN GATE's completeness check passes, dispatch the fresh-context `plan-reviewer`
subagent (it never sees the planning reasoning). The review's depth is right-sized to the
tier so blast-radius routing is preserved without dropping independent validation to zero:

- **`architecture` — full refutation.** The reviewer tries to refute the plan against the
  spec: hallucinated paths, weak/uncovered acceptance criteria, scope creep, missing edge
  cases, missing ADR for a hard-to-reverse decision. Returns `VERDICT: APPROVE | REJECT`.
  On REJECT: fix the plan and re-review. **Max 2 iterations**, then escalate to the user.

- **`standard` — lightweight coverage matrix.** The reviewer builds only the
  acceptance criterion → implementation task → test-plan matrix and flags any acceptance
  criterion with no covering task or no test. It does *not* hunt for scope creep or ADR
  gaps. Returns `VERDICT: APPROVE | REJECT`. On REJECT: fix the uncovered criteria and
  re-review **once**, then escalate to the user.

- **`trivial`** — skips this step.

This is distinct from the PLAN GATE: the gate is a structural completeness check (all 6
sections present) for every tier; this is an independent correctness check whose rigor
scales with the tier.

